	theme-role	surface
	pinnable	true
	layout	minimize,maximize,close,title-position
	behavior	drag,resize,maximize,minimize,close
	record-id	window-palette
# The pinned HUD subset (H-9.8): stays in the user's view while the shell is hidden.
#
# The four geometries below are the four corners of a 1280 × 720 window with the
# 48 dp bar across the top, sized so the panel each window hosts fits inside it:
# **the port's chrome — a 1 dp border, a 40 dp title bar and a 40 dp pane header —
# plus the panel's own height** (the tallest is 407 dp at seven rows — the World
# panel, which grew two rows when the player's body started reporting whether it
# was on the ground and whether it was in water). The chrome is the port's
# (SHELL-PORT.md §5; the reference always draws a pane header, 2670–2675) and it
# is 34 dp taller than the derived shell's title bar alone, so **the four corners
# no longer clear the middle of the screen**: the left column (489 + 342) is
# taller than the 672 dp a 720 dp viewport leaves under the bar, and the bottom
# pair is anchored to the viewport's foot as before (720 − height). Owed a
# ruling; the declaration is kept rather than an arrangement invented here. At
# any other window size the windows keep these declarations — a shell that
# resized them would be choosing an arrangement, and the arrangement is a package
# (UI-SPEC §3).
window	world
	title	World
	content	world-view
	lane	world
	extent	square-pixels
	geometry	16 48 336 489
	min-size	240 192
	opacity	930
	elevation	0
	theme-role	hud
	pinnable	true
	layout	minimize,close,title-position
	behavior	drag
	record-id	window-world
window	determinism
	title	Determinism
	content	readout
	lane	frame
	extent	square-pixels
	geometry	16 378 336 342
	min-size	240 192
	opacity	930
