	record-id	window-refusals
# Contextual tool layers (the Popit surface). A layer is declared beside its window and is
# drawn by the shell as the Popit grid; each action is routed back to the server as
# `layer:<window>:<action>`, and an action may also name a window to open locally first.
# This is the package's tool surface, not a second content page.
layer	inventory
	title	Inventory tools
	surface	grid
	hint	Select a tool, then a slot. The surface is data from this package.
	action	trees	Crafting trees	trees
	action	refusals	Refusals	refusals
	action	picker	Picker	picker
	action	reconcile	Reconcile
layer	mods
	title	Package tools
	surface	grid
	hint	A package is mounted by the server; these tools inspect what it delivered.
	action	uitree	UI tree	uitree
	action	settings	Settings	settings
	action	performance	Performance	performance
	action	picker	Picker	picker
layer	performance
	title	Measurement tools
	surface	grid
	hint	Readings are sampled while this window is open; the log keeps the last 64 entries.
	action	uitree	UI tree	uitree
	action	picker	Picker	picker
	action	reconcile	Reconcile
layer	map-plan
	title	Map tools
	surface	grid
	hint	Frame the live surfaces, or open the record views filed beside the map.
	action	skin	Popit surface
	action	minimap	Minimap	minimap
	action	world	World	world
	action	abilities	Abilities	abilities
	action	picker	Picker	picker
layer	docs
	title	Record tools
	surface	grid
	hint	The repository, landing page and update record are the motd addon's window shape.
	action	repo	Repository	repo
	action	landing	Landing page	landing
	action	updates	Updates	updates
	action	picker	Picker	picker
# The six tabs of the bar, in strip order (H-15.2).
tab	inventory
tab	trees
tab	mods
tab	docs
tab	settings
tab	map-plan
# The one bar entry that is not a tab.
bar	console
# What each tab's menu offers (H-15.3). The tab's own window is opened by the tab
# itself; these are the windows filed beside it.
filed	tools	inventory
filed	api-viewer	mods
filed	refusals	docs
filed	notifications	settings
filed	uitree	settings
filed	determinism	settings
filed	world	map-plan
filed	minimap	map-plan
filed	abilities	map-plan
filed	quickbuy	map-plan
filed	combat-log	docs
filed	game-settings	settings
filed	updates	settings
filed	performance	settings
filed	picker	settings
filed	repo	docs
filed	landing	docs
# Pinning is a layer move, declared here and not baked into a spec (UI-SPEC §4):
# a pinned window keeps the player's placement while the shell is hidden. The two live
# HUD elements are pinned by default; the record views are pinned where a player put them.

pin	minimap
pin	abilities
pin	refusals
pin	determinism


# The map window's content is a cell data frame, not composed panels. The row's id is the
# frame's id: `voxel_package::cellframe::read` refuses a declared frame this file names by
# no row, and `voxel-layers` prints both together so a reader can check the join.
row	MAP-0001	the map window's default cells: the world's own elevation and biomes, one sample a cell, with contours the mount grades before the shell draws one
row	MAP-0002	the ocean view: the measured map centred on the nearest water, water in accent and land in disabled ink
row	MAP-0003	the mountain view: alpine cells and high ground centred on the range the ring search found
row	MAP-0004	the forest view: the five forest biomes, centred on the nearest stand
row	MAP-0005	the grassland view: grassland cells, centred on the nearest grassland
row	MAP-0006	the desert view: desert and subtropical scrub, centred on the nearest dry ground
row	MAP-0007	the tundra view: tundra and polar desert, centred on the nearest cold ground
